Sure! Here's a simple HTML code for a web page with the heading "Welcome to our website":

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Welcome Page</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 100px 20px;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        h1 {
            color: #333;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to our website</h1>
</body>
</html>
```

### How to Use:
1. Copy the code above into a text editor (like Notepad, VS Code, etc.).
2. Save the file with a `.html` extension, for example: `index.html`.
3. Open the file in a web browser to see the result.

